File: src/lib/roster/rosterData.ts (main branch, 438 lines total). `listActiveMembers` spans lines 98-147:

```ts
export async function listActiveMembers(
	cfg: EntuCfg,
	fetchImpl: typeof fetch = fetch
): Promise<ActiveMember[]> {
	const res = await entuFetch(
		cfg.db,
		'entity?_type.string=member&status.string=active&props=person,_parent&limit=500',
		cfg.token,
		{},
		fetchImpl
	);
	if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`listActiveMembers failed: ${res.status}`);
	const body = (await res.json()) as {
		entities?: Array<{
			_id: string;
			person?: Array<{ reference: string }>;
			_parent?: Array<{ reference: string; entity_type?: string }>;
		}>;
	};
	return (body.entities ?? []).map((raw) => {
		const personId = raw.person?.[0]?.reference;
		if (!personId) {
			throw new Error(
				`listActiveMembers: member ${raw._id} — cannot read person reference (visible fields insufficient for this reader's rights; may be a narrower-than-entity sharing tier, not necessarily absent data)`
			);
		}
		const sectionIds = (raw._parent ?? [])
			.filter((p) => p.entity_type === 'section')
			.map((p) => p.reference);
		const dbEntityId = (raw._parent ?? []).find((p) => p.entity_type === 'database')?.reference;
		return {
			memberId: raw._id,
			personId,
			sectionIds,
			dbEntityId
		};
	});
}
```

CONFIRMED, precisely: an absent `person` reference on a `member` entity throws at rosterData.ts:123-127, inside the `.map()` callback processing `body.entities`, so it propagates synchronously out of `listActiveMembers`. `loadRoster` (line 346) `await`s that call with no try/catch around it, so a single member missing a readable person reference fails the ENTIRE collective's roster load. The issue's :118-127 citation is accurate for `listActiveMembers`, and the failure is not locally contained. Note this throw guards a different property (member's `person` reference) than #294's entu_user/join-state concern — it is unrelated to the redemption-state question but is a real existing fail-loud behavior.

rosterData.ts:174-210, verbatim:

```ts
export interface RosterRow {
	memberId: string;
	personId: string;
	name: string;
	email: string;
	sectionIds?: string[];
	dbEntityId?: string;
	profileName?: string;
}
```

Fields and provenance:
- `memberId` — the member entity's `_id` (from `ActiveMember.memberId`).
- `personId` — the linked person entity's `_id` (from `ActiveMember.personId`; required, throw-guarded per finding 1).
- `name` — the DISPLAYED name: domain-or-public profile name by default (`toRosterRow`, rosterData.ts:249), optionally overwritten by an admin_member_record real name when the #269 overlay applies (rosterData.ts:421-429).
- `email` — `resolveField(profiles, 'email').value`, narrower-wins across the member's domain/public profile tiers (rosterData.ts:250).
- `sectionIds?` — every section-typed `_parent` reference on the member, `[]` when unassigned, `undefined` only for pre-GREEN/legacy fixtures (rosterData.ts:180-187, 254).
- `dbEntityId?` — the member's collective (database-typed `_parent` reference), `undefined` when not visible to this reader or only a legacy `organization` parent exists (rosterData.ts:188-194, 256).
- `profileName?` — the roster's own domain-or-public profile name, carried separately from the possibly-overwritten `name` so out-of-scope surfaces (SectionPicker aria label, record-edit pencil, deactivate/damaged banners) keep naming the member by her profile identity even when the row displays a real name (rosterData.ts:195-209); set on every `loadRoster` row (rosterData.ts:355) equal to `name`, unset on `toRosterRow`'s bare output and on the separate inactive-roster loader.

No field carries any join/invitation/entu_user state today — RosterRow cannot express #294's three states without a new field.

