Each row is a `<li>` (flex column, dashed bottom border, line 3261-3264) containing: the name span (3265), an optional email span (3266-3268), an optional section span (3269-3271), then an admin-only block (3272 onward, gated `{#if admin === 'admin'}`) holding the record-edit pencil button and its inline editor. The admin-only deactivate controls (armDeactivate/disarmDeactivate) sit further down the same snippet (lines 3471-3560), also gated on `admin === 'admin'` and additionally on `row.personId !== selected?.personId` (never self-deactivate).

[speculative] A join-state badge attachment point: the badge DISPLAY itself would most naturally sit inline near the name/email spans (~line 3268), ungated on `admin === 'admin'`, consistent with the issue's finding that even a `_viewer`-level read returns the placeholder shape (so any roster viewer, not just admins, could in principle see it — though whether the product wants it visible to non-admins is a scope call this task doesn't answer). The `invite`/`reinvite`/`withdraw` ACTION controls, being admin mutations, would most naturally live inside the existing `{#if admin === 'admin'}` block (3272+), alongside the record-edit pencil and near the deactivate-button pattern (3490-3520) it can mirror structurally (armed/disarmed confirm state, per-row test ids). This placement judgment is mine, not sourced from the issue body or any code comment.

